      "text": "The Borrowed Dawn\n\nThe current evidence has been classified. Review its outcome and caveats before continuing.\n\nGame\nSound and reading\n\nThe beacon lights, and someone has the good sense to leave the temporary-route sign standing. Dawn has arrived on borrowed equipment. It is still dawn.\n\nYou leave two lines in the handover: service restored; permanent work outstanding. The second line is not a smaller victory. It is the reason tomorrow's engineer will know what to do before the borrowed installation must go home.\n\nSkip scene\n\nTemporary restoration: the borrowed bypass passed its physical checks and the separate endpoint service test. A temporary dependency remains.\n\nTemporary dependency: the tested bypass uses a borrowed installation in the protected work corridor. Limitation: this arrangement cannot be left as the permanent route. Follow-up: install and validate the permanent protected route before removing or returning the borrowed installation. Temporary service must pass the same fresh physical and endpoint checks.\n\nYour record follows the radio route through the Skywell and Storm Observatory. Signal and noise have separate places in the notebook. Neither was allowed to make a promise about service by itself.\n\nYou faced the Rift with your own observations and a well-used toolkit.\n\nThe main journey has a chapter of its own.\n\nThe borrowed-route handover stays tucked into your notebook, its limits and follow-up plainly marked.\n\nContinue returns to the safe Iron Threshold. The borrowed installation remains a temporary dependency; earlier rooms are still available.\n\nContinue"
    }
  ],
